Reduced volume `x = v/b`, `θ = R T b / a`, reduced pressure `π = p b² / a`. The PR isotherm is
`(a/b²) · g θ x` with `g θ x = θ/(x−1) − 1/(x² + 2x − 1)`;
`ψ θ π x = θ log(x−1) + (√2/4)(log(x+1+√2) − log(x+1−√2)) − π x` is a primitive of `g θ − π` on
`x > 1`. The derivative of `g θ` has the sign of `q θ x = (2x+2)(x−1)² − θ(x²+2x−1)²`, linear in `θ`.
For every `θ` in a narrow rational interval (endpoints in `reduced_window`) every Maxwell coexistence
state has its reduced pressure in a narrow rational window (`reduced_window`). Certificates:
`runs/2026-11-05T1228Z/scripts/gen_pr.py` (exact rationals); `√2` is enclosed between two rationals
and every certificate is monotone in it.
